[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435553 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6521128c-8b33-54da-8c83-d27bef687244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435529} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9c4d22-52c4-582f-b256-0ddd6fa135ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},1,-\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435530} {:answer/id #uuid "84cf53e7-7029-5a30-8dd0-ad54d0eb0064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435533} {:answer/id #uuid "bcd79e5d-b439-5f83-a72f-40d75fd4cdd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435537} {:answer/id #uuid "d89ebc6c-8c25-5ee8-a102-c0421505fca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{9}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d89ebc6c-8c25-5ee8-a102-c0421505fca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{9}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435540} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1008d1e-ad25-59f1-8249-03f1bd3c30fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0b70f07-48f3-5e91-bb4d-83ea4566f9c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-129560" :question/problem "At which point on the surface $z=4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}$ is the tangent plane perpendicular to the vector $v=⟨-2,-5,1⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhere $⟨\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}),-1⟩$ represents a normal vector to the tangent plane.\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2})=-4x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4-2{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2})=-10y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the normal vector to the tangent plane is \n\n$$\n⟨-4x,\\,-10y,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nOur tangent plane should be perpendicular to $⟨-2,-5,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of that plane must be parallel to that vector. In other words, for some constant $c$, we must have\n\n$$\nc\\cdot ⟨-4x,\\,-10y,\\,-1⟩=⟨-2,-5,1⟩.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coordinates, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4cx &=-2 \\\\ -10cy &=-5 \\\\ -c &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $c=-1.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-4(-1)x=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nAnd substituting $c=-1$ into the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n-10(-1)y=-5\\,⟹\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into our function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =4-2{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-5{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent plane is perpendicular to the vector $v$ at $(-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{9}{4}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ce76c4-9b3f-5e0d-8d4b-7dd6c7eb8a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,{\\theta }^{8}\\,{e}^{-2\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435563} {:answer/id #uuid "8a6185d9-5090-58f9-9faf-f0ca13d18ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,{\\theta }^{17}\\,{e}^{-8\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435573} {:answer/id #uuid "a64a48b1-2e38-5fa2-80c1-00ca67502114" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\theta }^{2}\\,{e}^{-17\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435575} {:answer/id #uuid "deae0969-c9d6-5654-be64-6233a00a8a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\theta }^{8}\\,{e}^{-17\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435583} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f696ee-8ecd-5fda-b688-f8cccd8853c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\,{\\theta }^{2}\\,{e}^{-8\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deae0969-c9d6-5654-be64-6233a00a8a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\theta }^{8}\\,{e}^{-17\\theta }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435583} :answer-field/id #uuid "75347981-9a28-5cb6-b027-b092523fc953" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83f5b615-5500-5815-8837-5144deae0691" :question/math-academy-id "q-159827" :question/problem "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{17}$ is an I.I.D random sample with ${X}_{i}∼Po(\\theta )$ and unknown rate parameter $\\theta .$ For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{17},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{17}{x}_{i}=8,\\,{\\prod }_{i=1}^{17}({x}_{i})!=4.\n$$\n\nFind the likelihood function of the sample.\n\n*Hint: The probability mass function for a Poisson distribution is given by* \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\theta }^{x}{e}^{-\\theta }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,…\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed discrete random variables with probability mass function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\nL(\\theta )={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=17$ independent Poisson random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability mass function is\n\n$$\nf(x;\\theta )=\\frac{{\\theta }^{x}{e}^{-\\theta }}{x!},\\,x=0,1,2,…\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can calculate the likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta ) \\\\  & ={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{i}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{i}!} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{1}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{1}!})\\cdot (\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{2}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{2}!})⋯(\\frac{{\\theta }^{{x}_{n}}{e}^{-\\theta }}{{x}_{n}!}) \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{\\sum {x}_{i}}\\cdot {e}^{-\\sum \\theta }\\cdot {\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{({x}_{i})!} \\\\  & ={\\theta }^{\\sum {x}_{i}}\\cdot {e}^{-n\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{{\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i})!} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{C}\\,{\\theta }^{S}\\,{e}^{-n\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i})!$ is a constant and $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}.$\n\nWe are told that $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}=8,$ $C={\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i})!=4,$ and $n=17.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(\\theta ) & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\theta }^{8}\\,{e}^{-17\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435630 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1733ba90-7a75-500a-9f67-81328a7b2bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435602} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4c96d9-6142-5eea-bb7d-cc2a65027b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435612} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c272ba-fbf8-56c8-83ab-774608b39901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435616} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2fd87e-1387-5790-9a23-44aec6dbd0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435617} {:answer/id #uuid "fda31041-af37-56fa-96cc-bf022686bc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc2fd87e-1387-5790-9a23-44aec6dbd0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435617} :answer-field/id #uuid "d783f8fb-1189-5732-8ecf-f5e33d4cb9ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e5fad29-e988-5832-87d5-889a9c3d0b32" :question/math-academy-id "q-132440" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{12}),$ what is $\\text{SD}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{12}),$ we have the following standard deviation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{5}{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "066b0a68-c03d-5252-a03f-d5dd1754583e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435600} {:answer/id #uuid "175f00cd-4983-5040-b101-e05b60df4667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435603} {:answer/id #uuid "486c46ba-79d7-5c83-a0d0-d5c2f86df67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435605} {:answer/id #uuid "db423d37-dc10-52d6-8943-139d912272ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435618} {:answer/id #uuid "e2271e40-5412-5ffe-a6c0-117c3cb78016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "486c46ba-79d7-5c83-a0d0-d5c2f86df67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435605} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a706a80-5de1-59dc-a5cd-a1ab263128d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "906813e4-c59b-59ab-b35c-7a3a5c47ebad" :question/math-academy-id "q-132438" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{11}{23}),$ what is $\\text{SD}[X]?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{11}{23}),$ we have the following standard deviation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{11}{23})} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b365ee9-c153-5ddd-a40d-da2203634354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.375" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b365ee9-c153-5ddd-a40d-da2203634354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.375" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435641} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8fee46f-9f97-52a3-886a-81612f3c88c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8e22e39-9704-57eb-a912-cb7e8741cbdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-331490" :question/problem "A fair coin is flipped $4$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability of getting heads exactly $2$ times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the coin lands on heads.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=4$ flips.\n\n- The probability of getting heads on a single flip is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(4,\\frac{1}{2}).$ We want to find the probability of $x=2$ successes.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}){(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4!}{2!(4-2)!}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =0.375,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435719 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bebf495e-8b3b-5a9d-a588-759127f24c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bebf495e-8b3b-5a9d-a588-759127f24c06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435704} :answer-field/id #uuid "dff647f1-983f-5ba6-9928-87a2fdcf179e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7130a2f-a2af-518c-8ac7-89bf1a4dc82f" :question/math-academy-id "q-343673" :question/problem "A particle of mass $0.5\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. An external periodic force $F(t)=-4sin\\,(\\frac{3}{2}t)\\,\\text{N}$ is applied to the particle.\n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in seconds. If the particle moves with forced harmonic motion without damping and the system experiences resonance, what is the spring constant $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}${\\text{kg/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of motion for a particle of mass $m$ moving with forced harmonic motion without damping under the action of a spring with spring constant $k$ and external force $F(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n0.5{y}^{″}=-ky-4sin\\,(\\frac{3}{2}t).\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2ky=-8sin\\,(\\frac{3}{2}t).\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ here represents simple harmonic motion, and it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration, and $\\omega $ is the system's internal frequency.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=2k\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{1}{2}{\\omega }^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe oscillator experiences resonance when the frequency of the external periodic force $f(t)=-8sin\\,(\\frac{3}{2}t),$ which is $\\frac{3}{2},$ is equal to the frequency of the complementary solution $\\omega .$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{1}{2}{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{9}{8}\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ccfe2f-0560-528d-ba84-ade4a43c6a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The domain is the entire $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435778} {:answer/id #uuid "6328591f-26cd-5a9c-bb16-a094d0fce559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le \\frac{1}{y-x}\\le \\pi \\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435781} {:answer/id #uuid "9d38eb2d-c186-5118-a6d9-96fbee67928e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le \\frac{1}{y-x}\\le 1,\\,y-x\\ne 0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435787} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea63572-0b73-594a-9be3-31c1af1775f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y-x\\ne 0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435789} {:answer/id #uuid "e3684b28-fb6d-5385-b110-85d8de2e97a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le \\frac{1}{y-x}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d38eb2d-c186-5118-a6d9-96fbee67928e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le \\frac{1}{y-x}\\le 1,\\,y-x\\ne 0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435787} :answer-field/id #uuid "4261be1e-d3be-5915-93ea-32ad8e744bfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04c36299-59f0-54ea-b2d4-6a2a60540beb" :question/math-academy-id "q-158583" :question/problem "Find the domain of the function  $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{y-x}).$" :question/worked-solution "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The argument of the arccosine has values between $-1$ and $1,$ and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-1<\\frac{1}{y-x}<1 \\\\ y-x\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-1\\le \\frac{1}{y-x}\\le 1,\\,y-x\\ne 0\\}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c9017c3-0305-5a1f-91b7-5ff0abefd2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435777} {:answer/id #uuid "4cdfbe0f-7325-5f77-a8c6-761b1ce65557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435779} {:answer/id #uuid "81903d38-806f-5011-865e-1ba6f995e0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435784} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf5fa64-468b-5aa3-b046-e9ca3d40c1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435786} {:answer/id #uuid "d978482b-dadc-5142-91af-61294dc15739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d978482b-dadc-5142-91af-61294dc15739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435794} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f239717-0131-5270-be88-b5cd8017e7fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb2bfb86-4e76-5321-aed7-06eaaf8188f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-158582" :question/problem "Evaluate $z=\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}$ at the point $(3,-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate our multivariable function at the point $(3,-\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ we substitute $x=3$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ into the function expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\,{|}_{(3,-\\pi /3)} & =\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}\\,{|}_{(3,-\\pi /3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "771854e8-d892-5203-a97d-09439ca5fe0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435979} {:answer/id #uuid "7efbea4c-7fba-5238-8596-49239d557793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435980} {:answer/id #uuid "8456a043-c86f-5008-9d67-2741aff12dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435981} {:answer/id #uuid "b334ddce-463a-5f5a-8086-6f71f3ca1947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435986} {:answer/id #uuid "e9634791-3b57-5087-836f-34d41f943f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8456a043-c86f-5008-9d67-2741aff12dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435981} :answer-field/id #uuid "49d01f52-f12f-5f40-8306-2b10fa6ebffd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab459c95-a786-5463-b6df-ba7f08de2795" :question/math-academy-id "q-109070" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{9}{2},$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X] & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{9}{2}.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+36\\cdot \\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X] & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436230 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a2bfeb5-10a6-5364-95db-232f11580849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436160} {:answer/id #uuid "534d1982-5794-5ef3-b6c7-550fa347ae5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436165} {:answer/id #uuid "b3684175-dfef-564c-9015-7ac3c04daa84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436191} {:answer/id #uuid "cc71899e-2b08-5805-bb87-08237cd8b8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436196} {:answer/id #uuid "e29dcf7e-fe90-5acc-b60e-5b9007f23b8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a2bfeb5-10a6-5364-95db-232f11580849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436160} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dda8d7f-6956-55ad-9209-2cf83e277760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ae1e8adc-b949-5f9d-889f-68a0d9d9eba2" :question/math-academy-id "q-144013" :question/problem "Three similar bags, $A,\\,B$, and $C,$ contain balls. Bag $A$ contains $4$ red and $6$ green balls, and bag $B$ contains $6$ red and $4$ green balls. A bag is selected at random, and a ball is randomly selected from the bag. If the probability that the selected ball is green is $\\frac{3}{5},$ what proportion of balls from bag $C$ are green?" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event of selecting a green ball at random from one of the three bags, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the ball is from bag $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the ball is from $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the ball is from bag $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a green ball, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $6$ green balls out of $10$ in bag $A,$ and $4$ green balls out of $10$ in bag $B,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{6}{10},\\,P(G|B)=\\frac{4}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability of choosing a green ball is $\\frac{3}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & =(\\frac{6}{10})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{4}{10})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(G|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{15}+(\\frac{1}{3})P(G|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{2}{15} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{4}{15} \\\\ P(G|C) & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{4}{5}$ of the balls in bag $C$ are green."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05abde05-5ea0-5346-b70b-e15ddb38a2b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436144} {:answer/id #uuid "18474b78-45ed-57a3-8328-b554a713c479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436147} {:answer/id #uuid "233072a2-5bde-566b-9863-22d8af3afca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436150} {:answer/id #uuid "5c42dd93-109c-5ae0-8799-e0b629f2949b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436168} {:answer/id #uuid "60c59049-514f-5905-b9eb-4d7a362f5ce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05abde05-5ea0-5346-b70b-e15ddb38a2b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436144} :answer-field/id #uuid "85fd5ffd-e434-5aa7-93f5-7f4265ffa862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca1787dc-fa3e-5ab1-99c5-cbfbd849d0c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-143747" :question/problem "Three bags contain marbles. Bag $1$ contains $12$ red marbles and $8$ green marbles. Bag $2$ contains $14$ red marbles and $6$ green marbles. And bag $3$ contains $10$ red marbles and $10$ green marbles. A bag is selected at random, and a marble is randomly selected from the bag. What is the probability that the marble is red?" :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be the event of selecting a red marble at random from one of the three bags, and\n\n- let $A$ be the event that the marble is from bag $1,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the marble is from bag $2,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the marble is from bag $3.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space.\n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a red marble at random from one of the three bags, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R) & =P(R\\cap A)+P(R\\cap B)+P(R\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|B)P(B)+P(R|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $12$ red marbles out of $20$ in bag $1,$ $14$ red marbles out of $20$ in bag $2,$ and $10$ red marbles out of $20$  in bag $3,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(R|A)=\\frac{12}{20},\\,P(R|B)=\\frac{14}{20},\\,P(R|C)=\\frac{10}{20}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability of selecting a red marble at random from one of the three bags is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(R) & =P(R|A)P(A)+P(R|B)P(B)+P(R|C)P(C) \\\\  & =(\\frac{12}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{14}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{10}{20})(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{60}+\\frac{14}{60}+\\frac{10}{60} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{60} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12065d32-e113-5992-bb8d-f535e75fb9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436257} {:answer/id #uuid "18efb766-1d3d-58da-bff5-d24f02292777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436258} {:answer/id #uuid "29173ece-c32d-5596-a3a8-34d0349c05ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436259} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a8b51a-6b08-55ab-89b7-ef577ff59874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436268} {:answer/id #uuid "b73c6eb0-be0e-57a4-8c3b-4e4f51c6378c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12065d32-e113-5992-bb8d-f535e75fb9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436257} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d69cbc-7ea6-5219-b9fe-b27e60e2aa63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c64c8376-4f9a-5df0-81b9-bf811d12f7ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-152904" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[4X+2].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of the expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[4X+2]=4\\text{E}[X]+2\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{0}^{1}+{(-\\frac{1}{2x})|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{8}-0)+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4X+2] & =4\\text{E}[X]+2 \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{7}{8}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30945d0b-c228-50cd-9399-4fc6759027b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436260} {:answer/id #uuid "477a366f-5027-5734-8066-1c5b19a5ae4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436262} {:answer/id #uuid "52eacba8-2ac3-5a25-85fe-9c675a072c68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436263} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffc82d5-d3b0-5643-95db-cbc049b36c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436264} {:answer/id #uuid "c10ec2db-f24e-557d-8a16-961d2cfcd677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30945d0b-c228-50cd-9399-4fc6759027b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436260} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9112695-ad08-5300-a06c-ea0b770acb45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "edac9b93-8284-5302-bc8b-9583d4ecc8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-152907" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[12X-8].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}, & 0<x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{8}{9}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the properties of the expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[12X-8]=12\\text{E}[X]-8\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{8}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{8x}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12})|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{12}-0)+(\\frac{16}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[12X-8] & =12\\text{E}[X]-8 \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{17}{12}-8 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436332 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19821da5-f0d9-5231-b6e6-57d05a583c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(x+h)^{y}+{x}^{y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436292} {:answer/id #uuid "31ac6394-634c-5df7-8435-c91eb48acad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(x+h)^{y}-{x}^{y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436295} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca1bb65-4836-5031-98cd-687ce371b497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{x}^{y+h}-{x}^{y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436296} {:answer/id #uuid "88c4c69c-b8ec-5afa-8545-f80894277b0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(x+h)^{y+h}-{x}^{y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436305} {:answer/id #uuid "dd81c589-9abe-5852-882a-90489739a54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{{x}^{y+h}+{x}^{y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31ac6394-634c-5df7-8435-c91eb48acad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(x+h)^{y}-{x}^{y}}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436295} :answer-field/id #uuid "76655532-0bc3-55d8-ba79-572397ad3e3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9785714b-27e4-57d0-bac5-65edf8d118a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-159575" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)={x}^{y},$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)={x}^{y},$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=(x+h)^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(x+h)^{y}-{x}^{y}}{h}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fd8c41-938d-5896-af76-a08ef933364a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436289} {:answer/id #uuid "14ea137a-7846-516f-9915-09b5b41d82fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xh-{y}^{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436291} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd25198-8ccd-5ecb-ab36-bbba0fbb0d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436297} {:answer/id #uuid "642b4c1b-1346-5ee7-abed-a5e7648fbb56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xh-{y}^{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436302} {:answer/id #uuid "959569af-b23a-5e0d-8446-2bab69573083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{h\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04fd8c41-938d-5896-af76-a08ef933364a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436289} :answer-field/id #uuid "25a45b6b-9452-510a-88d9-fa6cff3a05a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea65f87f-49a7-5b8c-93db-0d61d7663ef3" :question/math-academy-id "q-159576" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2}),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+h-{y}^{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{y}^{2})}{h}).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0966d4fd-1004-5375-90cf-1757ff705f99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)(y+h))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436290} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6f24d2-f9ef-5de6-894b-96a6e11cae68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy+h)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436303} {:answer/id #uuid "b4733487-8f20-5482-b97a-b62fc0d6cb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy+h)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436314} {:answer/id #uuid "dd8fe9b0-2dfe-5cce-8bde-270fb503d4de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436318} {:answer/id #uuid "e34026d0-8c07-5e65-85c3-9dc96c50dbd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x(y+h))-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd8fe9b0-2dfe-5cce-8bde-270fb503d4de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436318} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb776df8-d18c-56c6-b0af-71e18ee9b2ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fab082ec-08e1-574d-8102-367e3c718114" :question/math-academy-id "q-159572" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$ then $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(x+h,y)-f(x,y)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$  we have that \n\n$$\nf(x+h,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={lim}_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡((x+h)y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)}{h}).\n$$"}]
